The end of a turn hands the processor on without putting the thread whose turn it was back on its queue.
The thread would stay ready and never run again;
every ready thread but the running one that may run waits on a queue.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place of a ready thread that may run waits on no queue
Witness: fuzz actor-handoff

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1297,9 +1297,7 @@ void sched_turn_end(void)
     core->turn = NULL;
     core->turn_due = false;
     payer_drop();
-    if (was != NULL) {
-        thread_settle(was);
-    }
+    (void)was;
     core->turn = next_turn(now);
     run_turn();
 }
